        "original_id": "2e2b5443-adca-5117-aed4-6e3dddacadf9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Guiping, Hailin, Guangxi, Heilongjiang, northeast China\n- Rivers: Qian River, Yu Jiang, Xun, Xi Jiang\n- Transportation: Harbin–Mudanjiang Intercity Railway, Mudanjiang station\n- Cities: Harbin, Acheng, Maoershan, Shangzhi, Weihe, Yabuli, Hengdaohezi, Mudanjiang\n\nFacts:\n- Guiping is a county-level city in eastern Guangxi, China.\n- Hailin is a county-level city in Heilongjiang province in northeast China, and it is part of the prefecture-level city of Mudanjiang.\n- At Guiping, the Qian River is joined by the more southerly Yu Jiang to form the Xun branch of the Xi Jiang.\n- The Harbin–Mudanjiang Intercity Railway starts in Harbin and runs east through Acheng, Maoershan, Shangzhi, Weihe, Yabuli, Hengdaohezi, and Hailin before ending at Mudanjiang station.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
